visionOS VR R4 — hands: the viewmodel mount, the aim dot, delta-angles pitch, kick suppression

The shell owns everything it can (the Sense stack, the composition, the arbitration, the grip
rig). This is the residue that can only live in the engine, and it is four things:

  * THE HAND BLOCK in q2vr, appended. `hand_ofs` is in the IDENTICAL form as `eyeofs`, so the
    viewmodel mount is the eye composition with one substitution and hands, eyes and weapon
    are in one frame by construction rather than by two derivations agreeing. Two angle sets:
    `hand_ang` carries the grip calibration and places the MODEL, `hand_ray_ang` does not and
    is what the shot and the dot use — one set would make the gun and the bullet disagree by
    exactly the calibration.

  * THE VIEWMODEL MOUNT at the tail of CL_AddViewWeapon, so the face-attached placement above
    is overridden rather than fought and a mod's weapon lands in the hand for free. Weapon
    Size comes out of the renderer's own entity scale, which pivots about the entity ORIGIN —
    and the origin is now the grip point, so the slider pivots about the fist instead of about
    the player's face. That is the bug a donor shipped and then had to fix by subtracting an
    anchor before the multiply; here one point does both jobs. The muzzle flash is a separate
    timed entity in this engine, so there is nothing to cull — the one line that would undo
    the mount is the flash's reset to the VIEW angles, and that is now VR-gated.

  * THE DELTA-ANGLES PITCH COMPENSATION in CL_UpdateCmd. The server's view direction is
    viewangles + delta_angles. Yaw is already accounted for (the render adds the same term at
    the view.c site); pitch was not, because the render takes pitch from the pose. So an
    absolute pitch written here meant: die looking 35 degrees up, and for the rest of that
    life every shot leaves the barrel 35 degrees off, with nothing on screen to say so.
    `q2vrpitchcomp 0` restores the old behaviour exactly.

  * THE AIM DOT, a world point at the traced hit drawn through the existing particle pipeline
    — additive, billboarded, already scaled with distance (very nearly constant angular size).
    Deliberately not a GL line beam: Metal has no wide lines, and that is the feature both
    donors ended up deleting. Plus recoil kick suppressed under the VR gate, because in VR it
    is a camera moving in a way the player's neck did not ask for.

Every change is gated on `q2vr.active`, which no iOS, oracle or meson build ever sets.
